 "scope_note": "Table 2's Basel row (453/478 = 94.77% fact agreement) reproduces exactly by re-running regbench_basel/compute_basel_audit_summary.py. That figure combines two arms: 331/356 on the v5d-flagged items (v5d per-fact verdicts joined to reviewer labels) plus 122/122 on the 20-item v5d-pass sample (taken directly, no v5d join needed -- v5d passed those items and the reviewer marked every fact ok, so agreement is total by construction). Bridging to this log: 478 - 453 = 25 mismatches = 9 (v5d correct / SME defect) + 3 (same, with reviewers split) + 3 (v5d incorrect / SME ok) + 10 cells involving `ambiguous` or `uncertain`. The first 15 are the genuine conflicts, recorded here as 19 records because shared items are logged once per reviewer. The 10 ambiguous/uncertain cells count against the published agreement RATE -- that computation treats `ambiguous` as defect -- but are deliberately not conflicts here: a reviewer who could not decide has not contradicted the audit, and v5d expressing doubt has not asserted anything, since `uncertain` alone never flags. The published figure is regenerated by re-running regbench_basel/compute_basel_audit_summary.py."
